  "title": "Ecotone",
  "summary": "<em>An “ecotone” is a region of transition between two biological communities which is richer in species than both.</em><sup>1</sup> \r\n\r\nOur exhibition Ecotone distills the creative outflows of the Glitch community of artists and technologists. This growing network considers digital and natural ecologies to be innately entangled, with cross-border collaboration a vital means of generating new social realities. Involving over 60 participants from around the world, Glitch is a spectrum of strategies and a model for a new creator ecology — artistic, poetic, and human-machinic. \r\n\r\nFor this show with Feral File, Glitch is represented by a number of leading artists, whose range of approaches reflects the plurality of the community. Their works are the product of cross-pollination, and so a number of non-exhibitors have chosen to share their words here.\r\n\r\n<hr>\r\nGlitch is the scientists’ explanation of how life came into existence by a series of progressive chemical reactions and not by an act of God. But then, observe how we come together and merge creativity, our will, and the power of love to make the world a better place. Suddenly, we realize that we have created something new that survives us. The unpredictable timing of creative completion is proof of a divine force at play: it must be the Glitch.\r\n \r\n— Yessin Schiegg\r\n\r\n<hr>\r\nGlitch means multi-species connections, re-imagining nature and cities, and how we can find common ground in both our physical and digital states, in our cyborg bodies, aware of our own viscosity and our uncanniness, to form a network of solidarity. Glitch urges every cell of our anti-body to move and create in a constant state of interconnectivity. To me, that means restlessly sharing knowledge and creating experiences which encourage radical and sensual play.\r\n\r\n— Leonie Schramm\r\n\r\n<hr>\r\nÉcotone,\r\n \r\nNotre monde, notre climat, \r\nNotre communauté, Notre Écosystèmes,\r\nNotre Flux, Notre énergie, \r\nNotre Union, Notre harmonie,\r\nNotre convicti...",
